#
# Video calls over LTE on, over Wi-Fi off.
#
# The stock vendor declares persist.vendor.vilte_support=1 and
# persist.vendor.viwifi_support=1. Video over LTE needs two halves:
# vtservice_hidl in the vendor image, and vtservice, the system-side daemon,
# extracted from the stock system image with a shim for the framework symbols
# it lost (see proprietary-files.txt and shims/). Video over Wi-Fi needs Wi-Fi
# calling, which is off.
#
# Leaving a half on with nothing to answer it is not free. Without vtservice
# the radio daemon's RfxSender_11 thread spent all its time in
#
#   RmcVtReqHandler::handleRequestUpdateOpid
#     RmcVtReqHandler::sendMsgToVTS
#       usleep
#
# retrying a message to a video service that never answers: about 4800
# wakeups a second and 7.3 percent of a core, around the clock. With nobody to
# answer the Wi-Fi half the same would happen, hence the second property.
#
# Both values have to be forced, not just set once: vendor/build.prop defines
# the properties, and earlier builds of this tree saved vilte_support=0 in
# /data, which would otherwise outlive them. post-fs-data runs before
# class main, where the radio daemon (vendor.ril-daemon-mtk) starts; the
# trigger catches any later write of 1 to the Wi-Fi one.
#
# One more property, for video over LTE on networks MediaTek's dynamic IMS
# switch does not list for it, TIM's among them. ImsService asks the radio
# daemon, feature by feature, whether the operator supports it, and turns
# every one the daemon denies back off before it reaches the modem: the
# framework asked for video, the modem got AT+EIMSCFG=1,0,... With
# force.notify set, ImsService keeps the framework's value, and TIM accepted
# the registration with video (+CIREGU: 1,d) and a video call. Whether a
# carrier offers video is then down to its carrier config, as everywhere
# else in Android.
on post-fs-data
    setprop persist.vendor.vilte_support 1
    setprop persist.vendor.viwifi_support 0
    setprop vendor.ril.imsconfig.force.notify 1

on property:persist.vendor.viwifi_support=1
    setprop persist.vendor.viwifi_support 0
